<doc>Pre-processing rules applied before parsing to keep payload deterministic and free of inline documentation noise.</doc>
INSTRUCTION HYGIENE:
Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks from input payload before parsing (byte-stream safe).
Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks within CONFIGURATION section before parsing.

Treat every CONFIGURATION assignment whose resolved value is an empty
string as undefined.

Do not serialize undefined settings.

A module or container whose controlling ID is undefined must not be
created. Do not evaluate that module's nested mapping instructions.

Inside a collection loop, skip entries whose required configuration
values are undefined. Optional object properties may be omitted
individually.


<doc>Main configuration for schema, workshop metadata, transcript sources, and section delimiters.</doc>
CONFIGURATION:

<doc>Global context values used across extraction and language normalization.</doc>
{JSON_SCHEMA} = "ws_classes.schema.json"
{CUSTOMER_NAME} = "Tieto"
{TARGET_FILE} = lower({CUSTOMER_NAME}) + „_ws_results.json“
{LANGUAGE} = "English"
{INDUSTRY} = "Manufacturing"
{SYSTEM_CONTEXT} = ""
{COMMON_ABBREVIATIONS} = "KI, HCM, SAP"
{ABBREVIATION_CORRECTIONS} = "HCL->HCM, S.A.P->SAP, K.I->KI"

{WORKSHOP_DATE} = "2026-10-01"


